# Trivy vulnerability exceptions
#
# Scope: these five findings ONLY. Any other HIGH/CRITICAL finding still fails the
# "Docker build + scan" job in .github/workflows/application-ci.yml.
#
# All five are transitive Go dependencies compiled into the upstream FrankenPHP
# binary (usr/local/bin/frankenphp) via Caddy's certmagic/smallstep (ACME CA),
# OpenTelemetry OTLP exporter, and golang.org/x/crypto/ssh chains — not
# Laravel/Composer application dependencies, and not something this repo's
# Dockerfile/Caddy config can patch directly.
#
# Investigated 2026-08-29 (kin-openapi/grpc-go) and 2026-09-01 (x/crypto/ssh): no
# patched FrankenPHP release exists yet for either. Checked both the latest release
# (v1.12.7, 2026-08-07) and the unreleased `main` branch — both still pin
# github.com/getkin/kin-openapi v0.140.0, google.golang.org/grpc v1.81.1, and
# golang.org/x/crypto v0.54.0. dunglas/frankenphp:1-php8.4-alpine is a floating tag,
# so there's no newer image to bump to either.
#
# Reachability: this deployment runs `frankenphp php-server` with no custom Caddyfile
# and no OTLP/ACME/xDS/gRPC/SSH configuration anywhere in deploy/ or scripts/ (TLS is
# terminated by ingress-nginx, not Caddy). The vulnerable code paths are compiled in
# but not invoked by this application - CVE-2026-56854 specifically is an SSH
# *server* auth bypass, and this image never starts an SSH listener.
#
# Review by: 2026-09-28 (30 days). Re-run `docker build` + Trivy against the latest
# dunglas/frankenphp:1-php8.4-alpine on or before this date; remove any entry once a
# release fixes it, and re-investigate/extend only with a documented reason if not.

# kin-openapi: ValidationHandler.Load() Fail-Open (fixed upstream in 0.144.0)
